('রাজর্ষি (হিন্দি)', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Rajarishi_Hindi-Rabindranath_Tagore-89176-254451.jpg', 'রবীন্দ্রনাথ ঠাকুর', 'Fingerprint Publishing (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Novel', '9789389178210', 'Hindi', 152, '1st published 2019', 350.0, 350.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'While Raghupati, the priest of the Bhuvaneshwari Devi temple, believes that in order to please the goddess, a live sacrifice is essential, Raja Govind puts a ban on the practice. What follows is a struggle of power between the priest and the king. Raja Govind renounces his throne an becomes a Rajarshi, a royal sage. But he still hasn’t lost his kingdom. How will the Rajarshi emerge victorious? This classic book is a must-read for all! • It is written by the Nobel Prize Winner, Rabindranath Tagore • An entertaining tale on the practice of Bali • Highlights the richness of Hindi fiction stories • A story that will keep you hooked for hours • An excellent collectable for libraries and gifting'),
