('A Poet''s Mind: Selected Quotations', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/rokimg_20150524_99813.gif', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Times Group Books', 'Foreign Language Books : Poetry', '9788189906962', 'English', 70, '1st Edition, 2010', 288.0, 288.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('He (Shey)', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/rokimg_20140908_85354.gif', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Penguin group (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Childrens Fiction Books', '9780143102090', 'English', 152, '1st Edition, 2008', 625.0, 625.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('50 World’s Greatest Short Stories', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/50_Worlds_Greatest_Short_Stories-Mark_Twain-345dc-253394.jpg', 'Mark Twain , Rabindranath Tagore , James Joyce', 'Fingerprint Publishing (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Story', '9789386538277', 'English', 612, '20 January 2017', 598.0, 598.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Dating back to the early traditions of oral storytelling, the short story has evolved through the ages from myths, legends, fairy tales, fables, parables, stories in the Ramayana and Mahabharata, tales in the Panchatantra, the adventure tales of the Odyssey, biblical stories, the Norse sagas and many others. As the oriental tale and Gothic novel gained popularity in the latter half of the eighteenth century, short story began developing in Britain. And by the beginning of nineteenth century, it had highly evolved as a form. This anthology is a compilation of some of the classic short stories of the eighteenth and early nineteenth century, from around the world. Beginning with the realistic stories of Pushkin and Chekov, it includes ?The Necklace? by Guy de Maupassant, ?Eve?s Diary? by Mark Twain, ?The ?Slapping Sal?? by Arthur Conan Doyle, ?The Fly? by Katherine Mansfield, ?A Little Cloud? by James Joyce, ?White Nights? by Fyodor Dostoevsky, ?The Postmaster? by Rabindranath Tagore and ?The Gift of Magi? by O. Henry.?Short stories are tiny windows into other worlds and other minds and other dreams. They are journeys you can make to the far side of the universe and still be back in time for dinner.? ? Neil Gaiman??What shall I write?? said Yegor and he dipped his pen in the ink.?? Anton Chekov, At Christmas Time?There was a woman who was beautiful, who started with all the advantages, yet she had no luck.?? D. H. Lawrence, The Rocking-Horse Winner'),
('Essays On Tagore And Translation', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Essays_On_Tagore_And_Translation-Rabindranath_Tagore-ea79a-318934.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Birut Jtiyo', 'Foreign Language Books: Essay, Articles & Research', NULL, 'English', NULL, NULL, 900.0, 900.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Chitra - A Play in One Act', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/9336191f3_187834.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Niyogi Books (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Drama', '9789386906557', 'English', 56, '1st Edition, 2018', 1390.0, 1390.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Greatest Works of Rabindranath Tagore', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Greatest_Works_of_Rabindranath_Tagore-Rabindranath_Tagore-3cb4c-253499.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Fingerprint Publishing (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Essay, Articles & Research', '9789389053364', 'English', 672, '1st published, 2019', 1398.0, 1398.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'A compilation of the Nobel laureate’s literary masterpieces, this exquisitely designed leather-bound edition with gold gilded edges contains the English translations of his twenty-five classic short stories namely The River Stairs, The Postmaster, The Cabuliwallah, Living or Dead?, The Supreme Night, The Home-Coming, The Hungry Stones, The Auspicious Vision, Master Mashai, and Mashi among others. Also included is Gitanjali, his most celebrated collection of poetry; My Reminiscences, his memoir; and the well-known novel, The Home and The World. A small editorial note precedes each work.'),
('Baaghbaan', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Baaghbaan-Rabindranath_Tagore-f9ade-255493.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Harpercollins publishers (India)', 'Foreign Language Books : Poetry', '978935177785', 'English', 188, '1st edition: 2016', 1998.0, 1998.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Nindiya Chor', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Nindiya_Chor-Rabindranath_Tagore-bc401-255494.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Harpercollins publishers (India)', 'Foreign Language Books : Poetry', '9789351777830', 'English', 188, '1st edition: 2016', 1998.0, 1998.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Classic Rabindranath Tagore', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Classic_Rabindranath_Tagore-Rabindranath_Tagore-1fadf-340820.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Penguin Books (India)', 'Foreign Language Books', '9780143416326', 'English', 1136, '1st Edition, 2012', 2198.0, 2198.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Rabindranath Tagore experimented with form in his novels and was bold in his choice of subjects. This omnibus edition brings together the Nobel Prize winner’s most popular novels in translation. It is a collection that will be loved and treasured. A Grain of Sand (Chokher Bali), The Shipwreck (Noukadubi), Gora, Quartet (Chaturanga), Home and the World (Ghare Baire), Nexus (Yogayog), Farewell Song (Shesher Kabita), The Garden (Malancha), Four Chapters (Char Adhyay).'),
('Yogayog (Hindi)', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Yogayog_Hindi-Rabindranath_Tagore-77939-254475.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Fingerprint Publishing (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Novel', '9789389717587', 'English', 272, '1st published 2019', 398.0, 398.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Selected Stoies of Rabindranath Tagore B (PB)', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Selected_Stoies_of_Rabindranath_Tagore_B-Rabindranath_Tagore-71b7a-312275.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Rupa Publications (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Story', '9789357022248', 'English', 208, NULL, 500.0, 500.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Gora (Hindi)', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Gora_Hindi-Rabindranath_Tagore-fcd93-254472.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Fingerprint Publishing (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Novel', '9789389567175', 'English', 488, '1st published 2019', 500.0, 500.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('The Best Works of Rabindranath Tagore Boxed Set (Gitanjali, Nationalism, Selected Short Stories, The Home and The World)', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/The_Best_Works_of_Rabindranath_Tagore_Bo-Rabindranath_Tagore-ae6e5-517965.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Fingerprint Publishing (India)', 'Foreign Language Books', '9789362148049', 'English', 820, 'Edition, 2024', 1298.0, 1298.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Explore the best of Tagore''s literary world with this collection, including Gitanjali, a lyrical poetry anthology, enlightening essays on nationalism, and a range of his poignant short stories. Explore The Home and The World a novel that highlights themes of love, politics, and identity. Each book in this set offers a peek into Tagore''s exceptional insights into existence while celebrating his influence as one of India''s most prominent literary figures. Dive into love, politics, and identity galore. The collection features Tagore''s most cherished work, Gitanjali, which earned Tagore the prestigious Nobel Prize in Literature. Essays on nationalism offer a deep and nuanced exploration of this complex subject through Tagore''s insightful perspectives. Tagore''s poignant short stories showcase his mastery of the narrative form and his ability to evoke a range of emotions. Offers a glimpse into Tagore''s profound insights into the human condition, his lyrical language, and his talent for capturing the complexities of life. This boxed set allows appreciation for the breadth of Tagore''s literary contributions, showcasing his versatility as a poet, essayist, and storyteller.'),
('Gitanjali', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Gitanjali-Rabindranath_Tagore-acb45-340825.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Penguin (India)', 'Foreign Language Books', '9780143419563', 'English', 344, '1st Edition, 2012', 798.0, 798.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Gitanjali The paperback edition of the bestselling and acclaimed new translation by William Radice Described by Rabindranath Tagore as ''revelations of my trueself'', the poems and songs of Gitanjali established the writer''sliterary talent worldwide. They include eloquent sonnets such asthe famous ''Where the mind is without fear'', and poems that areintense explorations of love, faith and nature, and tenderevocations of childhood. William Radice''s new translation renders with beauty andprecision the poetic rhythm and intensity of the Bengali originals.In his arrangement of Tagore''s original sequence of poems alongsidehis translations, Radice restores to Gitanjali the structure, styleand conception that were hidden by W.B. Yeats''s edition of 1912,making this book a magnificent addition to the Tagore library. About the Author: William Radice William Radice is a poet and a scholar and translator ofBengali. He is well known for his translations of the poems,stories and plays of Tagore. He has recently translated The Poem ofthe Killing of Meghnad by Michael Madhusudan Dutt and a collectionof Tagore''s brief poems, The Jewel That Is Best, both for PenguinIndia. Reviews A towering figure in the millennium-old literature of Bengal''- New York Review of Books'),
('Sister Nivedita', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Sister_Nivedita_-Rabindranath_Tagore-eb387-541119.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Abhijan Publishers (India)', 'Foreign Language Books', '9789373632001', 'English', NULL, 'Edition, 2026', 400.0, 400.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Sister Nivedita emerges in this book as a remarkable intellectual and moral force whose life was devoted to India''s awakening. Through her close association with Rabindranath Tagore, Jagadish Chandra Bose, and other leading thinkers, and through the vibrant exchanges centered at 17 Bose Para Lane, the narrative reveals her deер engagement with art, science, education, and nationalism. Highlighting her crucial support of Bose''s scientific work and Tagore''s eloquent tribute, this volume offers a nuanced portrait of a woman driven by conviction, compassion, sacrifice and an unwavering commitment to India''s renewal.'),
('The Broken Nest', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/The_Broken_Nest_-Rabindranath_Tagore-2e860-568444.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Penguin Classics (India)', 'Foreign Language Books', '9780241752128', 'English', 128, 'Edition , 2025', 598.0, 598.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Rabindranath Tagore was one of the greatest authors of his generation. In these two short stories – ‘The Broken Nest’ and ‘Dead or Alive’ – he is at his devastating best, charting the slow, then fast, implosion of two perfect Bengali households. No-one understands each other; everything is misconstrued; all is lost.'),
('Songs of Kabir', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Songs_of_Kabir_-Rabindranath_Tagore-4741b-568127.jpg', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Fingerprint Publishing (India)', 'Foreign Language Books', '9789370899308', 'English', 112, 'Edition , 2026', 298.0, 298.0, '65%', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Songs of Kabirpresents the luminous poetry of one of India’s greatest mystic saints—a voice that speaks with startling directness about love, truth, illusion and the divine presence within. Kabir’s verses move beyond religious boundaries, rejecting empty ritual and outward display in favour of a deeply personal experience of God.Translated by Rabindranath Tagore, these songs carry both spiritual intensity and poetic grace. They ask readers to look inward, to question inherited divisions and to discover the sacred not in temples, ures or ceremonies alone, but in the living reality of the heart.Kabir’s poetry is simple yet profound, devotional yet rebellious, intimate yet universal. His words challenge hypocrisy, ego and spiritual pride, while offering a path of love, awareness and surrender. Each song becomes a call to wakefulness—a reminder that the divine is not distant but present in everyday life.Perfect for readers of spiritual classics, poetry and Indian philosophy, Songs of Kabir remains a timeless work of mystical wisdom and inner freedom.'),
